comment.narrative:
There are seven facilities that have been designated for the acute care of COVID-19 cases, namely Jui&nbsp;Chinese hospital, 34 military hospital,&nbsp;Kenema government hospital,&nbsp;Makeni government hospital,&nbsp;Lungi,&nbsp;Bo government hospital and Kailahun government hospital. All designated COVID-19 Healthcare facilities have isolation capacity. It should be noted that there are no government standards that specify the requirements that need to be met to comply with this indicator.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

As of December, 2022, 90 percent&nbsp;of people reported having adequate knowledge on Infection Prevention and Control (IPC) measures and vaccine efficacy.

During the last quarter, a community perception survey was conducted by the MoHS, NACOVERC and other partners like FOCUS1000, IGR, and Health for All. According to the survey&#39;s report, 90 percent&nbsp;of females have adequate knowledge on preventive measures.

A new citizen perception survey is underway and new figures will be available by June 15th.&nbsp;
